<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18479" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφρᾰδ-ία</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ιη,</span>
		ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>folly, thoughtlessness,</i> in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always in dat. pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνέρος ἀφραδίῃσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.649
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιμένος ἀφραδίῃσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					16.354
				</span></i>
			; exc. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι᾽ ἀφραδίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					19.523
				</span></i>
			, and 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφραδίῃ πολέμοιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.368
				</span></i>
			.—
				Ep.
			 word, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφροσύνη</span> being
			used for it in Prose; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφραδίῃσι</span>
			in a mock heroic line, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				1064
			</span></i> (hex.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
